{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he shall bring it before YHWH and make atonement for her and she shall be cleansed from the flow of her blood</b> — it means that she shall bring the ransom of her soul before YHWH so that she shall be cleansed from the flow of her blood. For the woman in childbirth has a weakened spring and a corrupted flow, and after she has stood through the days of her purification — whether the days of formation of the offspring, for male or for female — she shall bring the ransom of her soul so that her flow may cease and so that she may be cleansed, for HaShem, exalted, heals all flesh and works wonders.\n\nAnd our Sages said (Niddah 31a): At the time she crouches to give birth she clenches and swears: 'I will not again be intimate with my husband.' And the essential intention in this is that because she swears out of pain, and the oath is not fit to be upheld since she is subjugated to her husband, the Torah sought to make atonement for her to calm her spirit. And the thoughts of HaShem, blessed, are deep, and His mercies are abundant, for He desires to justify His creatures."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:53:13.011426924Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}